    dict(key='04-act-1', kind='console', title='Act One — A tag made with a shared key',
         body='ONE. A tag made with a shared key.\n  the shop tags its price list with HMAC: 2efbd273904d2215\n  the warehouse must be able to check the tag, so it holds the same key\n  the warehouse tags a list of its own, with the laptop at 12 dollars: accepted  <- ANYONE WHO CAN CHECK CAN FORGE',
         narration="First demo: a tag made with a shared key. [[slnc 400]] This is H M A C, from the earlier video. [[slnc 600]] The shop tags its price list with a secret key. [[slnc 300]] The warehouse must be able to check tags, so it holds the same key. [[slnc 600]] That means the warehouse can also make a tag. [[slnc 300]] It tags a list of its own, with the laptop at twelve dollars. [[slnc 300]] And the shop's check accepts it. [[slnc 600]] Anyone who can check, can forge. [[slnc 300]] For a few services that trust each other, that may be fine. [[slnc 300]] For anything wider, it is not."),
